        "title": "Lumina Shader - Event Horizon",
        "description": "A next-generation cinematic shader pack designed to deliver uncompromising graphics, advanced lighting, and deep environmental immersion for high-end setups.",
        "body": "Lumina Shader: Event Horizon is a complete cosmic and visual overhaul for Minecraft, specifically engineered for players who refuse to compromise on cinematic realism and high performance.\n\n✨ Why Lumina: Event Horizon?\nUnlike basic profile edits, Lumina introduces advanced, custom-coded features that provide a distinct filmic identity:\n\nThe End Overhaul (Gargantua): A movie-accurate analytical black hole featuring a sharp accretion disk, realistic gravitational lensing, and a stable world-space rendering engine.\n\nDynamic White Hole & Anamorphic Flares: A stunning cosmic counterpart in the End dimension with custom cinematic lens flares.\n\nProcedural Atmospheric Flicker: A custom time-based light flickering effect for deeply immersive environments.\n\nCinematic Grain & Post-FX: A dynamic noise generator combined with custom vignette curves for a true film texture.\n\nOptimized Lighting: Fine-tuned volumetric God Rays with manual PCF 2x2 filtering, targeting a smooth 100-150 FPS experience.\n\n📜 Credits & License\nMain Developer: Benjiaa\n\nIMPORTANT: This shader is based on Complementary Shaders by EminGT. Special thanks to him for his incredible work and for allowing the community to build upon his foundation.\n\nOriginal Project: https://modrinth.com/shader/complementary-reimagined\n\n💬 Support & Community\nIf you enjoy the cosmic journey of Lumina, consider supporting my work! You can find dev logs, report bugs, and see early previews here:\n\nhttps://github.com/benjamincalledur10-bit/Lumina_Shader_Event_Horizon/issues\n",
